# 1. DOCUMENT PURPOSE

## 1.1 Objective

This document defines the approved target system architecture for Kea Parrot.

It establishes the architectural boundaries, application layers, infrastructure, service responsibilities, data flows, integration patterns, security boundaries, realtime architecture and deployment model required to build Kea Parrot as a production-ready application from a greenfield start.

The document is an implementation contract for the engineering team and AI coding agents.

It must be used alongside the Kea Parrot Master PRD.

## 1.2 Architectural principle

Kea Parrot must be developed as a modular monolith with clearly separated business domains.

The application must remain straightforward to develop, test, deploy and maintain without introducing unnecessary distributed-system complexity.

The architecture must support future expansion without requiring an early migration to microservices.

## 1.3 Important implementation rule

This document defines the target architecture for a greenfield build. No prototype
exists (confirmed by the owner 2026-11-20): there is no existing repository,
infrastructure, or implementation to inspect, preserve, or migrate. Product P0 is a
greenfield foundation phase, not a prototype-to-production audit (D-04).

Preservation rules (no destructive operations, no disabling RLS, no inventing
requirements) still apply — to all work from Product P1 onward. Nothing is preserved
because nothing exists yet.

Do not claim in any phase report that an existing system was audited in this repo.
When the first implementation is created in Product P0, verify it against this target
and record any deviation with its cost, risk, and approval before changing it.

Never introduce complexity simply to match a preferred folder structure or
architectural pattern.

