# 5. MODULAR DOMAIN ARCHITECTURE

Each business domain must have a defined responsibility.

## 5.1 Identity module

Responsibilities:

- Authentication integration.
- Session validation.
- User identity resolution.
- Account lifecycle.
- Role and permission resolution.

It must not independently duplicate Supabase Auth's credential management.

## 5.2 Profiles module

Responsibilities:

- User profiles.
- User preferences.
- Profile visibility.
- Profile updates.
- User blocking relationships.

Private identity information must remain separate from public profile information.

## 5.3 Discovery module

Responsibilities:

- Nearby feed.
- Global feed.
- Trending feed.
- Content filtering.
- Feed pagination.
- Location-aware discovery.

Feed ranking must use approved and documented rules.

No undisclosed AI recommendation system is permitted in the MVP.

## 5.4 Social module

Responsibilities:

- Posts.
- Anonymous posting.
- Reactions.
- Comments.
- Content visibility.
- Ownership checks.

Anonymous content must remain associated with an authenticated internal account. Guests cannot post, so anonymous posting is authenticated-only (Guest Session Rule, §9.4).

## 5.5 Polls module

Responsibilities:

- Poll creation.
- Poll options.
- Vote validation.
- Vote submission.
- Poll expiration.
- Results calculation.

The database remains authoritative for votes and results.

Vote replacement (D-11, decided 2026-11-20): a registered user may change their vote
while a poll is open — one active submission per user per poll; changing replaces the
previous submission atomically; no change after close/expiry. A guest may NOT change
or remove a vote: one final submission per guest session per poll. Guest voting
follows the Guest Session Rule (§9.4): one vote per poll per guest session, within a
60-minute participation window; guest votes are counted.

## 5.6 Games module

Responsibilities:

- Game definitions.
- Question retrieval.
- Game sessions.
- Answer validation.
- Scoring.
- Completion status.

Scoring must be calculated and validated on the trusted server side.

Guests may play the 3 games within the Guest Session Rule (§9.4): a guest game session
is tied to the guest session only, never to an account; guest scores are not saved to
a profile and do not appear on leaderboards.

## 5.7 Communities module

Responsibilities:

- Community records.
- Community memberships.
- Membership validation.
- Community-linked discovery.

Only approved MVP community functionality may be implemented.

## 5.8 Locations module

Responsibilities:

- Approved location records.
- User-selected areas.
- Approximate location handling.
- Geospatial queries.

Exact user coordinates must not be publicly exposed.

No background location tracking is permitted.

## 5.9 Notifications module

Responsibilities:

- Notification generation.
- Notification persistence.
- Read and unread states.
- Notification preferences.
- Delivery coordination.

## 5.10 Moderation module

Responsibilities:

- User reports.
- Content review.
- Moderation decisions.
- Enforcement actions.
- Blocking-related workflows.
- Moderation audit records.

## 5.11 Administration module

Responsibilities:

- Administrative dashboards.
- User management.
- Content management.
- Moderator management.
- Platform configuration.
- Audit-log access.

Administrative permissions must be enforced independently of frontend visibility.

## 5.12 Analytics module

Responsibilities:

- Approved application events.
- Product usage measurement.
- Aggregated engagement reporting.
- Operational analytics.

Analytics must not become a mechanism for collecting unnecessary sensitive user information.

