# 14. DISCOVERY AND FEED ARCHITECTURE

## 14.1 Feed types

Kea Parrot supports:

- Nearby.
- Global.
- Trending.

## 14.2 Feed retrieval

The discovery module retrieves approved content through the application data-access layer.

Requirements:

- Cursor-based pagination.
- Visibility filtering.
- Moderation filtering.
- Efficient database queries.
- Stable pagination.
- Appropriate indexes.
- No duplicate records during ordinary pagination.

## 14.3 Trending

Trending must use documented and approved ranking logic.

Potential inputs established in the product requirements include:

- Recency.
- Engagement.
- Unique participants.
- Moderation signals.
- Spam indicators.

Exact coefficients and thresholds must not be invented (TBD — see README Open Decisions register).

## 14.4 Location-aware discovery

Location-aware discovery must:

- Support manual area selection.
- Support permission-based approximate location where approved.
- Work when location permission is denied.
- Avoid background tracking.
- Avoid public exposure of exact coordinates.
- Apply approved geographic search limits.

