# 15. MONITORING AND OBSERVABILITY

The application must provide visibility into technical health.

## 15.1 Error monitoring

Sentry is the approved initial monitoring option.

Capture:

- Frontend exceptions.
- Backend exceptions.
- Failed API operations.
- Important background job failures.
- Performance problems.
- Deployment-related failures.

## 15.2 Structured logging

Logs should include:

- Timestamp.
- Environment.
- Severity.
- Application module.
- Operation.
- Request identifier.
- Relevant diagnostic context.

Do not log secrets, passwords, session tokens or unnecessary sensitive data.

## 15.3 Operational metrics

Monitor:

- Application availability.
- API latency.
- Error rates.
- Database health.
- Realtime health.
- Background job failures.
- Authentication failures.
- Storage usage.
- Core user journeys.

Detailed monitoring thresholds will be finalised in KEA-TPR-005 (TBD — see README Open Decisions register).

