## 16.3 CI/CD requirements

The pipeline must verify, in this order (D-07 merged CI list):

1. Dependency install.
2. Formatting.
3. Linting.
4. Type checking.
5. Unit tests.
6. Component tests.
7. Integration tests.
8. API tests.
9. Database & RLS tests.
10. Production build.
11. Security & dependency scans.
12. Migration validation.
13. Deployment checks.
14. Post-deployment smoke tests.
15. Required approval gates.

Failed critical gates must block release; pipelines must not silently ignore failing
critical tests.

## 16.4 Database migrations

All schema modifications must be version-controlled.

Production migrations require review and approval.

The application must not automatically perform destructive schema changes during normal startup.

## 16.5 Recovery

Document:

- Application rollback.
- Database backup.
- Database restoration.
- Migration recovery.
- Credential rotation.
- Incident response.

Never assume a database rollback is safe when it may discard user-generated data.

