# 17. PERFORMANCE AND SCALABILITY

The initial performance objectives are:

| Metric | Target |
|---|---|
| LCP | ≤ 2.5 seconds at p75 |
| INP | ≤ 200 ms at p75 |
| CLS | ≤ 0.1 at p75 |
| Standard read API latency | p95 below 500 ms under agreed workload |
| Poll update latency | Normally within 2 seconds |

These are targets, not claims of existing performance.

## 17.1 Scaling strategy

Initial scaling should focus on:

- Efficient queries.
- Correct indexes.
- Cursor pagination.
- Small API payloads.
- Optimised rendering.
- Appropriate caching.
- Connection management.
- Realtime subscription efficiency.

Do not split the application into microservices without measurable evidence and an approved architecture change.

## 17.2 Capacity planning

Expected concurrent users, request rates, database capacity and realtime connection targets must be established before production load testing (TBD — see README Open Decisions register; do not invent).

