# 20. ARCHITECTURAL ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA

The architecture is accepted when:

- [ ] All major business domains are identified.
- [ ] Module responsibilities are documented.
- [ ] Dependencies between modules are understood.
- [ ] Trusted and untrusted execution boundaries are defined.
- [ ] Authentication and authorisation boundaries are documented.
- [ ] PostgreSQL is established as the authoritative persistent data store.
- [ ] Realtime architecture is documented.
- [ ] Background processing responsibilities are documented.
- [ ] API boundaries are defined.
- [ ] Storage access boundaries are defined.
- [ ] Monitoring responsibilities are defined.
- [ ] Deployment environments are documented.
- [ ] Migration and recovery principles are established.
- [ ] The Product P0 greenfield implementation has been verified against the target (no existing architecture exists to compare — D-04).
- [ ] Material architecture changes have approval.
- [ ] No unresolved critical architectural risks remain.

